2026-10-28T17:15:40.7696201Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgV1hJ8hFQmDQraEa1N14","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016DJuZs53SQc2orZpZQUfyH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":24855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6008,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78aa36ee-f9ff-4876-8d43-f89931e47a8b","uuid":"06b3dace-9391-48d5-8608-8ed2c966ece7","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:15:40.767Z","request_id":"req_011CgV1hHn83EvyGcYHEwHvF"}
2026-10-28T17:15:40.7863140Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016DJuZs53SQc2orZpZQUfyH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 9,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/9\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_bedrockagentcore_memory_strategy fails with \\\"Value Conversion Error\\\" on configuration.type (OverrideType) for SUMMARY_OVERRIDE strategies\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```console\\nTerraform Core Version\\n1.15.8\\n\\nAWS Provider Version\\n6.47.0\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n`aws_bedrockagentcore_memory_strategy`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nA CUSTOM memory strategy configured with a SUMMARY_OVERRIDE configuration block (built-in strategy with a custom consolidation prompt) should plan and apply cleanly, and should be readable back into state on subsequent plans/refreshes.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nAny operation that materializes the resource into the provider's type model \\u2014 `plan`, `apply` (post-create read-back), or refresh of existing state \\u2014 fails with a `Value Conversion Error` on `configuration[0].type`. The provider receives a `null` value for the `OverrideType` field and cannot decode it.\\n\\nThe failure occurs during state/response decode, so it is not avoidable via -`refresh=false` (prior state is still decoded) or `lifecycle { ignore_changes = ... }` (the error precedes diff computation). Built-in strategies without a `configuration` block (e.g. `type = \\\"SEMANTIC`\\\") are unaffected, because there is no `OverrideType` to decode.\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output\\n\\n```\\n\\u2502 Error:   : Value Conversion Error\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2502   with aws_bedrockagentcore_memory_strategy.short_term_room[0],\\n\\u2502   on agentcore-memory.tf line 62, in resource \\\"aws_bedrockagentcore_memory_strategy\\\" \\\"short_term_room\\\":\\n\\u2502   62: resource \\\"aws_bedrockagentcore_memory_strategy\\\" \\\"short_term_room\\\" {\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2502 Cause: An unexpected error was encountered trying to build a value. This is\\n\\u2502 always an error in the provider. Please report the following to the provider\\n\\u2502 developer:\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2502 Received null value, however the target type cannot handle null values. Use\\n\\u2502 the corresponding `types` package type, a pointer type or a custom type that\\n\\u2502 handles null values.\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2502 Path: configuration[0].type\\n\\u2502 Target Type: types.OverrideType\\n\\u2502 Suggested `types` Type: types.StringEnum[github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/service/bedrockagentcorecontrol/types.OverrideType]\\n\\u2502 Suggested Pointer Type: *types.OverrideType\\n\\n```\\n\\n\\n### Sample Terraform Configuration\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand configuration</summary>\\n\\n```\\nresource \\\"aws_iam_role\\\" \\\"memory_exec\\\" {\\n  name = \\\"agentcore-memory-exec-repro\\\"\\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\\n    Version = \\\"2012-10-17\\\"\\n    Statement = [{\\n      Effect    = \\\"Allow\\\"\\n      Principal = { Service = \\\"bedrock-agentcore.amazonaws.com\\\" }\\n      Action    = \\\"sts:AssumeRole\\\"\\n    }]\\n  })\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_bedrockagentcore_memory\\\" \\\"short_term_room\\\" {\\n  name                      = \\\"repro_short_term_room_memory\\\"\\n  description               = \\\"Repro - short-term room memory\\\"\\n  memory_execution_role_arn = aws_iam_role.memory_exec.arn\\n  event_expiry_duration     = 7\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_bedrockagentcore_memory_strategy\\\" \\\"short_term_room\\\" {\\n  name        = \\\"room_session_summary_strategy\\\"\\n  description = \\\"Summarises recent conversation with a custom English-only consolidation prompt\\\"\\n  memory_id   = aws_bedrockagentcore_memory.short_term_room.id\\n  type        = \\\"CUSTOM\\\"\\n\\n  namespaces = [\\\"rooms/{actorId}/sessions/{sessionId}/\\\"]\\n\\n  memory_execution_role_arn = aws_iam_role.memory_exec.arn\\n\\n  configuration {\\n    type = \\\"SUMMARY_OVERRIDE\\\"\\n\\n    consolidation {\\n      append_to_prompt = \\\"Always summarize in English regardless of the input language.\\\"\\n      model_id         = \\\"eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\nSteps to Reproduce\\n`terraform apply` the configuration above. The strategy is created in AWS, but the post-create read-back fails with the `Value Conversion Error` above (the resource may be left created in AWS but absent/tainted in state).\\nAlternatively, for a strategy already present in state, run `terraform plan` \\u2014 it fails on the same decode while reading prior state (also fails with `-refresh=false`).\\n\\n### Debug Logging\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand log output</summary>\\n\\n```console\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### GenAI / LLM Assisted Development\\n\\nn/a\\n\\n### Important Facts and References\\n\\nImportant Factoids\\n\\n- The equivalent built-in strategy (`type = \\\"SEMANTIC\\\"`, no configuration block) works fine, isolating the issue to the `configuration.type (OverrideType)` decode path used by the `*_OVERRIDE` strategy types.\\n- The API/CloudFormation model supports `SUMMARY_OVERRIDE` with a `consolidation` block, so the configuration itself is valid \\u2014 this appears to be a provider-side decode issue where a null `OverrideType` from the API response cannot be handled.\\nWorkaround: use a built-in `type = \\\"SUMMARIZATION\\\"` strategy with no `configuration` block, which sidesteps the decode path but loses the custom consolidation prompt.\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [\n10\t    \"bug\"\n11\t  ],\n12\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:07:59Z\",\n13\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-07-22T13:14:57Z\"\n14\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78aa36ee-f9ff-4876-8d43-f89931e47a8b","uuid":"c397f846-afe7-4d6e-a400-3cff36519b09","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:15:40.780Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 9,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/9\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_bedrockagentcore_memory_strategy fails with \\\"Value Conversion Error\\\" on configuration.type (OverrideType) for SUMMARY_OVERRIDE strategies\",\n  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```console\\nTerraform Core Version\\n1.15.8\\n\\nAWS Provider Version\\n6.47.0\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n`aws_bedrockagentcore_memory_strategy`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nA CUSTOM memory strategy configured with a SUMMARY_OVERRIDE configuration block (built-in strategy with a custom consolidation prompt) should plan and apply cleanly, and should be readable back into state on subsequent plans/refreshes.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nAny operation that materializes the resource into the provider's type model \\u2014 `plan`, `apply` (post-create read-back), or refresh of existing state \\u2014 fails with a `Value Conversion Error` on `configuration[0].type`. The provider receives a `null` value for the `OverrideType` field and cannot decode it.\\n\\nThe failure occurs during state/response decode, so it is not avoidable via -`refresh=false` (prior state is still decoded) or `lifecycle { ignore_changes = ... }` (the error precedes diff computation). Built-in strategies without a `configuration` block (e.g. `type = \\\"SEMANTIC`\\\") are unaffected, because there is no `OverrideType` to decode.\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output\\n\\n```\\n\\u2502 Error:   : Value Conversion Error\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2502   with aws_bedrockagentcore_memory_strategy.short_term_room[0],\\n\\u2502   on agentcore-memory.tf line