\\n  type        = \\\"CUSTOM\\\"\\n\\n  namespaces = [\\\"rooms/{actorId}/sessions/{sessionId}/\\\"]\\n\\n  memory_execution_role_arn = aws_iam_role.memory_exec.arn\\n\\n  configuration {\\n    type = \\\"SUMMARY_OVERRIDE\\\"\\n\\n    consolidation {\\n      append_to_prompt = \\\"Always summarize in English regardless of the input language.\\\"\\n      model_id         = \\\"eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\nSteps to Reproduce\\n`terraform apply` the configuration above. The strategy is created in AWS, but the post-create read-back fails with the `Value Conversion Error` above (the resource may be left created in AWS but absent/tainted in state).\\nAlternatively, for a strategy already present in state, run `terraform plan` \\u2014 it fails on the same decode while reading prior state (also fails with `-refresh=false`).\\n\\n### Debug Logging\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand log output</summary>\\n\\n```console\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### GenAI / LLM Assisted Development\\n\\nn/a\\n\\n### Important Facts and References\\n\\nImportant Factoids\\n\\n- The equivalent built-in strategy (`type = \\\"SEMANTIC\\\"`, no configuration block) works fine, isolating the issue to the `configuration.type (OverrideType)` decode path used by the `*_OVERRIDE` strategy types.\\n- The API/CloudFormation model supports `SUMMARY_OVERRIDE` with a `consolidation` block, so the configuration itself is valid \\u2014 this appears to be a provider-side decode issue where a null `OverrideType` from the API response cannot be handled.\\nWorkaround: use a built-in `type = \\\"SUMMARIZATION\\\"` strategy with no `configuration` block, which sidesteps the decode path but loses the custom consolidation prompt.\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"bug\"\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2